WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.980
On November 20, 2022, news broke&nbsp;
that actor and martial artist Jason&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:09.660
David Frank died at 49 years old. While&nbsp;
Frank's acting career spanned decades,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:13.620
his best-known work was playing the Green and&nbsp;
White Rangers in the original "Mighty Morphin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:18.300
Power Rangers" TV series. News of Frank's&nbsp;
death hit fans hard, given the important&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:22.260
part he played in the franchise's early&nbsp;
popularity and subsequent development.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:27.240
Frank's life even mirrored that of the Green&nbsp;
Ranger, in that both he and his most well-known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:32.340
character ended up succeeding in unlikely ways. In&nbsp;
"Power Rangers" canon, the Green Ranger starts off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:37.080
as a villain, before overcoming his evil influence&nbsp;
and eventually leading the Power Rangers team.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:41.400
Frank, meanwhile, initially signed on for&nbsp;
just 10 episodes of "Power Rangers," but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:45.420
ultimately became so popular he stuck&nbsp;
around not just for the balance of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:50.040
original "Power Rangers" show but for a number of&nbsp;
subsequent incarnations of "Power Rangers" also.

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:54.360
Of course, Frank booked the Green Ranger role&nbsp;
in the first place at least partially on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:58.500
strength of his martial arts abilities. In&nbsp;
fact, Frank's martial arts expertise nearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:04.000
landed him in a fight with noted action movie star&nbsp;
Jean-Claude Van Damme on two separate occasions.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:05.280
"I don't want to hurt you."

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:09.236
"Me? You don't want to hurt Hank?"

00:01:09.236 --> 00:01:13.920
In November 2017, combat sports blog&nbsp;
FloCombat published a history of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:18.720
contentious relationship between Frank and&nbsp;
Van Damme, including some direct quotes from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:23.460
Frank himself explaining how their dynamic&nbsp;
twice nearly erupted into full-on fights.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:27.540
First, Frank met Van Damme, who he had&nbsp;
idolized, at a "Power Rangers" event in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:34.080
1995. Frank found Van Damme rude, and in 2010&nbsp;
issued a challenge to fight Van Damme in an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:38.820
organized mixed martial arts match. This first&nbsp;
possible fight, however, never came to fruition.

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:42.960
Then, backstage at a Comic Con&nbsp;
event in 2017, after both actors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:46.980
finished scheduled appearances, Van Damme&nbsp;
approached Frank alongside his entourage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:51.180
seemingly looking to provoke the Green Ranger&nbsp;
into hitting him. Frank told FloCombat,

00:02:00.103 --> 00:02:03.120
Shortly after that, Comic Con&nbsp;
security separated the two men.

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:07.680
A Daily Mail piece about this incident notes&nbsp;
that Frank also challenged Herschel Walker and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:11.940
pro wrestler CM Punk to fight him as well.&nbsp;
Whereas nothing came of these challenges,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:15.420
however, his beef with Van Damme&nbsp;
culminated in a face-off seven years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:18.360
later that nearly blew up into a backstage brawl.

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:22.200
According to Frank's account, the aggressor&nbsp;
in the situation was Van Damme. Frank,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:26.280
meanwhile, had previously suggested the two&nbsp;
compete in a sanctioned MMA competition.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:30.960
Despite the nature of this experience, Frank&nbsp;
maintained that he held no ill will toward Van&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:34.740
Damme in its aftermath. In a Facebook post&nbsp;
shortly after news of the incident broke,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:38.940
for example, Frank encouraged fans of Van&nbsp;
Damme's films to continue to appreciate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:42.480
his body of work without letting the&nbsp;
near-fight influence their opinion.

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:47.700
Frank also discussed their combative history&nbsp;
during a Q&amp;A at a 2021 Comic Con event. A&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:51.900
fan asked Frank if he's still interested in an&nbsp;
organized bout with Van Damme. Frank responded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:55.560
that, while he's game, his only interest in&nbsp;
the fight would be to raise money for charity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:58.440
given that he holds no ill will&nbsp;
toward Van Damme personally.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:03.360
While Frank's disappointment with Van Damme as&nbsp;
an individual dated back to 1995, the "Power&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:07.871
Rangers" star was adamant about separating&nbsp;
the artist from his art in his final years.

